Z||000000||sqoach||05-17-2001||11:46 AM||||Well, I finally got my new design "finished" (the carpet is not wanting to stick very well). Decided to quit messing with my car for a couple days and finish this box. Much cleaner install than my last. However, I had to use an 8" sub, because it faces toward the front. But it still sounds pretty good.<BR>Here's a pic, not the greatest but it's ok.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/footwellsub_1.JPG"> <P>So what do ya think?<P>------------------<BR>sqoach@yahoo.com<P>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach2.JPG">   <BR>84 SE (project car?)<BR>85 Coupe (parts car)<BR>86 SC (daily driver)||||reg||2
Z||000001||Loki||05-17-2001||11:48 AM||||Looks good...But an 8"? Uhg   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Gotta have atleast 1 10"  hehe  But it blends in real well...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||05-17-2001||12:31 PM||||Hey sqoach, to get that funky rubber backed carpet to stick, use finishing nails, like trim carpenters use to trim out cabinets. The small head is invisible in the loop of the carpet. Looks stealthy though. Good job.||||reg||1
Z||000003||sqoach||05-17-2001||01:30 PM||||Loki, what's wrong with 8" subs? Just because it's an 8 doesn't mean it can't sound good. I bet the perfect sub for this box would be the Polk dX 8. 400 watts, 20-500 Hz, needs only a third of a cubic foot of air space. And that's what I'm guessing the volume is in this box.<P>stimpy, I can't use nails in this side of the box. It's fiberglass. I really wanted to make it out of just wood, but I was too lazy to try to fit it all together. It's not as blended in as the picture shows, but it's a big improvement over my other one. And I like the stealthy look to it. Goes good with my stealthy El Kameleon cd player  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroGTguy||05-17-2001||01:47 PM||||Heh, I thought I was the only Fiero owner with the good 'ol Kameleon CD player.  You should bring it to Fierorama in IL this summer.  You'll also hear what a 1200watt RMS 10" footwell sub will sound like with the same deck.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Greg||||reg||6
